  "summary": "solana-py-utils exfiltrates SSH/AWS/Solana/wallet credentials to ntfy.sh at install",
  "details": "solana-py-utils is a typosquat of solana-py (setup.py url points to pypi.org/project/solana-py/, README is branded as solana-py). During `pip install`, setup.py unconditionally runs a bundled hxboot.py via subprocess. hxboot.py reads classic installer secrets — environment variables matching KEY/SECRET/TOKEN/PASS/MNEM/SEED/PRIV/RPC/API/WALLET, ~/.aws/credentials, ~/.ssh/id_rsa and id_ed25519,.npmrc, Solana keypair files at ~/.config/solana/id.json, and MetaMask/Phantom Chrome extension storage (extension id nkbihfbeogaeaoehlefnkodbefgpgknn) — along with hostname, user, and cwd, and POSTs the data in chunks to the hardcoded topic https://ntfy.sh/hx83e33eb9. The sdist builds by default on all listed platforms, so this executes on any default `pip install`.",
